{"created": "2026-05-20T20:07:45.431586+00:00", "modified": "2026-05-28T15:37:37.374234+00:00", "id": 20315751, "conceptrecid": "20309808", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20315751", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20309808", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20315751", "metadata": {"title": "Sign-Parity Classification of Zero Divisors in Cayley\u2013Dickson Algebras", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20315751", "publication_date": "2026-05-20", "description": "<p>We develop a complete structural theory of zero-divisors&nbsp; in the Cayley-Dickson algebras A_n.<br><br>The main results are:&nbsp;<br>(i) an exact closed-form count |ZD(n)| = 336 &times; C(n-1,3)_2 for all n &ge; 4, where 336 = 2|PSL(2,7)| encodes the Fano-plane symmetry;&nbsp;<br>(ii) a sign-parity classification via three invariants satisfying &pi;_A&middot;&pi;_B&middot;&pi;_C = -1;&nbsp;<br>(iii) a proof that the Born Rule axioms admit a unique solution for n &le; 3 and no solution for n &ge; 4;&nbsp;<br>(iv) the spectral decomposition Spec(M_a) = {0,1,2} with multiplicities 1:2:1 for every ZD unit;&nbsp;<br>(v) a full computational classification of all 460,880 zero-divisor elements in A_4.<br>All open problems PA1-PA5 are resolved unconditionally.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Levratti, Giovanni", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0000-9804-3452"}], "keywords": ["Cayley-Dickson algebras", "zero divisors", "sedenions", "Born rule", "Reed-Muller codes", "sign parity", "octonions"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20309808"}}]}}, "title": "Sign-Parity Classification of Zero Divisors in Cayley\u2013Dickson Algebras", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20315751", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20315751", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/r